course: dictionary
lesson: 8691
title: Two meanings of seizure
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Seizure» has two meanings, so context tells you which one is meant. Read the words around it first.
explain: In health and safety lessons, a seizure is a sudden burst of unusual electrical activity in the brain. It can make a person shake, fall, stare or lose consciousness. «A seizure is a sudden burst of electrical activity in the brain that can make the body shake.» Epilepsy is a condition that can cause seizures.
explain: In the news, «seizure» means taking something by force or by law. «The police seizure of stolen goods» is about police taking things, not about a person's body. Ask yourself: is someone unwell, or are things being taken? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it.
fact: A seizure is a sudden burst of unusual electrical activity in the brain.
fact: If someone has a seizure, keep calm, move hard things away and never hold them down.
fact: During a seizure, never put anything in the person's mouth.
fact: Time the seizure, and get an adult or call 999 for help if it lasts more than five minutes.
fact: «Seizure» can also mean taking something by law, as in «the drug seizure» when police take illegal drugs.
exercise: «During a seizure, keep the person safe by moving hard things away.» What is the best first step? | Shout at them to stop | *Move hard things away | Hold them down tightly | Put a spoon in their mouth
exercise: «The police made a seizure of stolen goods.» What does seizure mean here? | A sudden shake of the body | A short holiday | A brain puzzle | *Taking something by force or by law
exercise: «Dafydd's brother has an epileptic seizure at the park.» What does epileptic seizure mean? | A sudden burst of laughter | *A sudden burst of unusual electrical activity in the brain | A bad cold | A long walk in the rain
test: Which statement about a seizure is true? | *It can make a person shake, fall, stare or lose consciousness | It is always a kind of holiday | It is a happy surprise
test: «The seizure of the drugs was in the news.» What does seizure mean? | A fit of giggles | *Taking something by force or by law | A long rest | A kind of sweet
exam: In a seizure, what should you never do? | Time how long it lasts | Move hard things away | *Hold the person down
